{"id": "EUVD-2026-93111", "enisaUuid": "7292a597-8365-3eb9-abc9-6455045d27df", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mac80211: avoid out-of-bounds read for empty PREQ elements\n\nieee80211_mesh_preq_size_ok() derives the location of the PREQ bottom\nfields before checking whether the element contains even the fixed\nheader. ieee80211_mesh_hwmp_preq_get_bottom() reads the flags byte to\naccount for the optional Address Extension field. Consequently, an\nempty PREQ element causes a one-byte read beyond its declared payload.\n\nMove the helper call after both size checks, so the bottom fields are\nonly accessed when they are present.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:44:26", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:15:14", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3beddbd56946577478fd5e649f556aaaebe15b0a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e6031f02269c0f51cf67886d177f02bc300b47cd"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98183", "GHSA-867h-2x92-cj79"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "42e3b1df-2497-3bd8-a035-49adecb219ca", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8b40b1d24a6099fe9fac8e207d4cb04ab5e0baae <3beddbd56946577478fd5e649f556aaaebe15b0a"}, {"id": "69f4393e-e46e-373c-ba38-c8af99c158e9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8b40b1d24a6099fe9fac8e207d4cb04ab5e0baae <e6031f02269c0f51cf67886d177f02bc300b47cd"}, {"id": "84e89299-bb04-35f5-83ce-c8f35d81d4fd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "e280aee1-0a91-387c-a27f-957f709882c2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7.2"}, {"id": "e40184fb-89ee-3720-9087-9290af560445", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "f91c185b-8b39-35b2-bfbf-c182f7e2be20", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "1890e6d4-b8bd-3d23-9faf-34a7c136604a", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}